py-mir-toolbox
==============

py-mir-toolbox is a Python port of MIRtoolbox. Its code is translated from
MiningSuite, the BSD-licensed successor of MIRtoolbox.

MiningSuite
-----------
Copyright (C) 2014-2015, 2017-2018 Olivier Lartillot and the MiningSuite contributors.
Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License (see reference/miningsuite/LICENSE.txt).
Upstream: https://github.com/olivierlar/miningsuite (commit 7b3e4688b2b33e1d3b8c580c95e518457a4ee627)
Packages used: +sig, +aud, +mus

MIRtoolbox
----------
MIRtoolbox 1.8.2, Copyright (C) 2023 Olivier Lartillot, University of Jyväskylä,
University of Geneva, University of Oslo. Developed by Olivier Lartillot,
Petri Toiviainen, Pasi Saari et al. Licensed under GPL-2.0.
Upstream: https://github.com/olivierlar/mirtoolbox

MIRtoolbox source code is NOT included in or translated into this package.
MIRtoolbox 1.8.2 is used only as a numerical reference: outputs are compared
against it in the validation suite. The MIRtoolbox manual is used as documentation.

Data files
----------
Key profiles (gomezprofs.mat) and the key self-organizing map
(keysomaudiodata.mat) come from MiningSuite (+mus) under its BSD license.

